ents in skidrow before they attain citizenship <br /> <br /> <b>Judicial Hearings</b><br /> <br /> 1. Every citizen is entitled to a single vote.<br /> <br /> 2. The same item may only be voted on once per five year period.<br /> <br /> 3. Titles are granted via a general vote of the city populace.<br /> <br /> 4. Laws may be added, removed, or changed via a general vote of the city populace.<br /> <br /> 7. When a law change is being voted on, the proceedings are guided by all available members of the Judicial Council.<br /> <br /> 8. Once every four months, a Court is held as an opportunity to debate and vote on a suggested law or changes.<br /> <br /> 9. At each Court, people place suggested additions or changes where the populace pics what will be voted on at the next court.<br /> <br /> 10. You may not sabotage a Court or its proceedings.<br /> <br /> <b>Trial Laws</b><br /> <br /> 1. A trial is a special kind of Court used to determine the guilt and possible punishment given to the accused.<br /> <br /> 2. The populace votes on the suggested treatment of the accused as presented by the prosecution and defense.<br /> <br /> 3. The Court is preceded over by a recognized judge who is considered by the judicial council acceptably distant from those involved in the trial.<br /> <br /> 4. When no neutral judge can be agreed upon, multiple judges may be used to ensure fairness.<br /> <br /> 5. A matter can only be brought to trial once and is considered resolved thereafter.<br /> <br /> 6. Information obtained through the use of disciplines may be used to help an investigation but is considered less reliable than witness testimony.<br /> <br /> <b>Skid Row Laws</b><br /> <br /> 1. Residents may not take the life of Kindred.<br /> <br /> 2. Residents may not drink the blood of Kindred.<br /> <br /> 3. To gain citizenship, a citizen, who is not your sire, must sponsor your application into the city. It is put to a vote if another citizen objects to your admittance.<br 